### Cost Efficiency Analysis
**Source:** Multiple sources
**Snapshot:** 2026

Muse Wonder's real cost efficiency depends on:
- Prompt caching usage (80% cost reduction on input tokens)
- Batch API usage (not specified)
- Effort level selection (higher effort = more thinking tokens = higher cost)
- Task complexity and length
- Context length (1M tokens)
- Task type (agentic workloads benefit from memory features)

The model is positioned as Meta's flagship general-purpose model for personal and professional AI agents. The cache-read pricing is 80% cheaper than standard input pricing ($0.20 vs $4 per 1M tokens), cutting typical workload costs by approximately 80% and highly agentic workloads by up to 90%.

